---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Service journalism, sourced from our dossier: remove.bg's own banner,
// terms and announcement as read 7 November 2026, and its shutdown FAQ as
// reported by Photoroom (29 October 2026), AI Tools Police (26 October
// 2026) and Hokai (read 28 October 2026). Items only reported second-hand
// are marked as reported, not stated.
const closes = [
  ['The website', 'The standalone remove.bg site stops being available at 09:00 CET on 1 December 2026. Background removal moves into Canva. (remove.bg banner and terms, read 7 November 2026.)'],
  ['Accounts', 'Accounts end with the site. Subscriptions end automatically, with no further charge. (Shutdown FAQ, as reported.)'],
  ['Every unused credit', 'All remaining credits expire at that moment, subscription credits and pay-as-you-go credits alike, including pay-as-you-go credits that were sold as never expiring. No refund for unused pay-as-you-go credits has been reported. (Shutdown FAQ and reporting, as reported.)'],
  ['The self-service API', 'API keys stop working. API users are pointed to Leonardo.Ai, which is also owned by Canva.'],
  ['Plugins and apps', 'The Photoshop plugin and the other integrations and plugins stop, and so do the desktop and Android apps, which depend on the API. (Shutdown FAQ, as reported.)'],
];
const todo = [
  'Use your credits before the date, or accept losing them. They do not move to Canva and they are not refunded.',
  'Download anything you still need from your account: past results, invoices, settings. The account ends with the site.',
  'If your product calls the API, plan the move now. The official destination is Leonardo.Ai; keys for remove.bg stop working on the day.',
  'Pick the tool your hands will use next and try it on a real photo before the date, not after it.',
];
---

<Base title="What happens to remove.bg on 1 December 2026 · Benchzy" description="What closes, what happens to unused credits, where the API goes, and what to do before 1 December 2026. Dated facts from remove.bg's own announcement and terms, read November 2026.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">Explainer · facts checked 8 November 2026</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black mt-2">What happens to remove.bg on 1 December</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        remove.bg, the best-known background remover, is closing its standalone site on
        1 December 2026 at 09:00 CET. The job itself moves into Canva, where background removal
        is a paid-plan feature. This page is the plain list of what ends, what happens to money
        already spent, and what to do before the date. Facts are from remove.bg's own banner,
        terms and announcement as read on 7 November 2026; where a fact comes from reports of
        its shutdown FAQ, the line says "as reported".
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">What ends</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
        {closes.map(([what, detail]) => (
          <article class="ticket-soft p-5">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold">{what}</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mt-1">{detail}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-xs text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
        One line in the reporting is not confirmed by remove.bg's own pages: that enterprise API
        contracts continue past the date. Treat that as reported, not settled, and ask the
        company directly if it is your contract.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">What to do before 1 December</h2>
      <ol class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
        {todo.map((t, i) => (
          <li class="ticket-soft p-4 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <span class="text-accent-deep font-bold">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')} ·</span> {t}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="ticket mt-10 p-6 mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">After the date</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft max-w-2xl">
        The habit has to live somewhere. The official home is Canva; the fuller list, with each
        option's wall marked from its own terms, is our
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/remove-bg-alternatives/">remove.bg alternatives</a> guide.
        Our own tool does the job free, at full size, in your browser:
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/remove-background/">remove a background</a>.
        That is the only sales line on this page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
